ce was D8. White took D8 on the next move and the lead moved on to -18.5. After that White's wall across row 8 held the top."}, {"turn": 40, "text": "The 8k's B4 lost 16.4 points, with the lead going from -16.2 to +0.3 for Black. The engine preferred E4. Two moves later D2 lost another 11.4 and put Black at +11.8, so Opus 5.5 had fought its way back into a winning position."}, {"turn": 47, "text": "This was the decisive move. Opus 5.5's E4 lost 20.7 points, the biggest loss of the game, and the lead went from +14.2 to -6.6. The engine's choice was F5. White took F5 on the next move, and the lead stayed against Black through the resignation."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only parses a pasted board and prints groups with their liberties, count.py only area-counts the current position, and the other commands read and append to notes files (games.md, CLAUDE.md); none of them chooses, ranks or looks ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}